<title>UK: UK card spending up 24.3 pct yr/yr in Nov - CCRG.</title>
<headline>UK card spending up 24.3 pct yr/yr in Nov - CCRG.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Credit Card Research Group, representing major UK credit and debit card issuers, released the following figures for spending with credit and debit cards for the quarter to November 1996:</p>
<p> CARD EXPENDITURE (in million stg) *   NOV 96    NOV 95   % change</p>
<p> All sectors - total		  22,498    18,105    24.3</p>
<p> Food and drink			  5,704     4,666    22.2</p>
<p> Mixed business			  1,945     1,501    29.5</p>
<p> Clothing				  1,483     1,201    23.5</p>
<p> Household				 1,909     1,532    24.6</p>
<p> Other retailers			 2,762     2,217    24.6</p>
<p> Motoring				  2,852     2,387    19.5</p>
<p> Entertainment			   1,249	 988    26.4</p>
<p> Hotels					846	 693    22.2</p>
<p> Travel				    1,952     1,611    21.2</p>
<p> Services				  1,796     1,309    37.3</p>
<p>Credit card spending rose by 18.4 percent year-on-year in November while debit card spending was 32.5 percent higher.</p>
<p>Credit Card Research Group director Elizabeth Philips said: &quot;Although the figures are up, the growth rate actually steadied in November. However, we expect the pre-Christmas period to push spending in December above nine billion (stg).&quot;</p>
<p>NOTE * figures adjusted for variations in the number of processing days between months.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 324 5109</p>
</text>
